{% comment %} Section: FAQs (Accordion) {% endcomment %}
<style>
  .faq-section {
    background-color: #11151a;
    padding: 64px 24px;
    width: 100vw;
    position: relative;
    left: 50%;
    margin-left: -50vw;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .faq-section__inner {
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .faq-section__category {
    margin-bottom: 44px;
  }

  .faq-section__category:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .faq-section__category-title {
    font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #d4af37;
    margin: 0 0 16px 0;
    padding-bottom: 12px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #2a2f38;
  }

  .faq-section__list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .faq-section__item {
    border: 1px solid #2a2f38;
    background-color: #1a1f27;
    border-left: 3px solid #2a2f38;
  }

  .faq-section__item.is-open {
    border-color: #d4af37;
    border-left: 3px solid #d4af37;
  }

  .faq-section__header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 18px 22px;
    cursor: pointer;
    -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;
  }

  .faq-section__question {
    font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #ffffff;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .faq-section__toggle {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 1px solid #d4af37;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    transition: transform 0.25s ease;
  }

  .faq-section__toggle svg {
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    color: #d4af37;
  }

  .faq-section__item.is-open .faq-section__toggle {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .faq-section__body {
    max-height: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: max-height 0.3s ease;
  }

  .faq-section__body-inner {
    padding: 0 22px 20px 22px;
  }

  .faq-section__answer {
    font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #aaaaaa;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .faq-section {
      padding: 48px 16px;
    }

    .faq-section__category {
      margin-bottom: 32px;
    }

    .faq-section__category-title {
      font-size: 11px;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
      padding-bottom: 10px;
    }

    .faq-section__list {
      gap: 10px;
    }

    .faq-section__header {
      padding: 14px 16px;
      gap: 12px;
    }

    .faq-section__question {
      font-size: 14px;
      line-height: 1.4;
    }

    .faq-section__toggle {
      width: 24px;
      height: 24px;
    }

    .faq-section__toggle svg {
      width: 10px;
      height: 10px;
    }

    .faq-section__body-inner {
      padding: 0 16px 16px 16px;
    }

    .faq-section__answer {
      font-size: 13px;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 420px) {
    .faq-section {
      padding: 40px 12px;
    }

    .faq-section__header {
      padding: 12px 14px;
    }

    .faq-section__question {
      font-size: 13.5px;
    }
  }
</style>

<div class="faq-section">
  <div class="faq-section__inner">

    <div class="faq-section__category">
      <h3 class="faq-section__category-title">Opening The Safe</h3>
      <div class="faq-section__list" data-faq-list>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">How do I dial in, as well as, change the S&amp;G SPIN DIAL combination?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Make sure the door handle is firmly down, then turn the dial left to stop at your first number the fourth time, right to the second number the third time, left to the third number the second time, and right slowly until it stops around 85-86. Finally, lift the handle firmly. A video demonstration is available on our site — just substitute your actual numbers for the example “50-25-50.”</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">How do I dial in, as well as, change the combination of a D-Drive S&amp;G ELECTRONIC dial?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">The factory combination is “123456#” followed by turning the ring right until it stops. To change it, make sure the door is open with the handle down, hit “22*” plus your current code and “#” (five beeps), enter your new 6-digit code and “#” (three beeps), then re-enter it and “#” again (three more beeps).</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">Do you offer a redundant dial?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">No. The manufacturer previously discontinued redundant locks due to the poor longevity of their electronic components, which failed prematurely despite costing $350. They now recommend the Sargent and Greenleaf D-Drive electronic lock instead, which has fewer moving parts and a longer lifespan.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">I dialed in right, I have the right combination, but it still won't open!? (For S&amp;G Spin Dial and Securam)</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">A few things to check: make sure the dial reaches a complete stop at 96 in step five; push the handle down harder before dialing (fire-lined safes have stiffer handles); try adding or subtracting a number from your combination; or try the jiggling and tapping method at positions 10, 5, and 0. For electronic dials, note that three failed attempts trigger a 15-minute lockout.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-section__category">
      <h3 class="faq-section__category-title">General Safe Information</h3>
      <div class="faq-section__list" data-faq-list>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">What is the fire rating without fire protection?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Non-insulated safes have performed reasonably well during real fires, with response times around 13 minutes. The larger size and thicker steel of the body help delay heat buildup. Ceramic wool liners or a UL-rated fire box can be added inside an uninsulated safe for extra protection if needed.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">Why shouldn't I get my safe fire lined?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Fire-lining adds cost, so it may not be worth it if insurance covers your contents, you're within five miles of a fire department, your safe is in a low-burn zone with sprinklers, or you won't be staying in that location long-term. In those cases, a smaller UL fire box placed inside works better than an inferior thin-steel fire-lined alternative.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">Do you sell the fire liner separately, as a kit?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">No, fire liner kits are no longer available for separate purchase.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">Which package should I get? What are the benefits of adding more steel?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Thicker steel means more security and a longer breach time. What you should choose depends on the tools a burglar might realistically have access to, whether you have an alarm system, how quickly emergency responders reach you, how often the home is occupied, and fire risk from grinding or torch use. Higher burn-zone areas make torch-based breaching less likely due to fire risk.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">What kind of paint do you use?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">We use a water-borne, semi-gloss enamel that's sprayed on for excellent durability.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">What does your warranty cover? Why is it better?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Full details are on our dedicated warranty page — our coverage is built to be stronger than what most competitors offer.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">Why should I go with Sturdy Safe?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Five reasons: thicker steel at lower prices than competitors; genuine fire insulation sourced from actual kiln and oven manufacturers, which is lightweight and effective; deadbolts and linkage that withstand repeated door slamming without lockouts or damage; multiple finish options that add real security through steel plating; and unique offerings like floor plates and security door covers you won't find elsewhere.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">Where can I see the safe in person? Do you have any dealers?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">We have one dealer: Heavy Metal Gun Safes in New Braunfels, Texas. We primarily sell direct-to-consumer to keep pricing low, but safes can also be viewed at our Fresno, CA warehouse. We're happy to provide comprehensive documentation, videos, and pictures on request.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">Have one of your safes been successfully broken into? How?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Yes, three break-ins have occurred. We're upfront that no safe is truly “impenetrable” — be skeptical of any brand that claims otherwise. Most of these breaches involved torch methods, often using the owner's own torch against them.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">Is your safe water proof or water resistant?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Be skeptical of any manufacturer's “true waterproof” claims. The best flood protection comes from placing the safe on a pedestal, rather than relying on sealed construction alone.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">Do you store the combination?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Yes, in coded form, and it's accessible only to the original owner — we never disclose it to third parties, even by warrant. Older safes may not have a stored code on file. Ultimately, remembering your combination is the owner's responsibility.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">Where is the serial number on the safe?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">We have never put serial numbers on our safes. For registration purposes, use the model number and our company name instead. We meet or exceed all DOJ requirements.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">How many deadbolts are there?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Four stationary deadbolts on one side and four moving deadbolts on the other — none on top. This is sufficient because each side's deadbolts are fully supported, preventing deviation even under 10,000 pounds of pulling force.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">What type of stainless and/or carbon steel do you use?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">We use A36 to Grade 50 carbon steel and 304 stainless steel.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">How long is the Dri Rod cord?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Dri Rod cords are approximately 6.5 feet long.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-section__category">
      <h3 class="faq-section__category-title">Unloading And Moving</h3>
      <div class="faq-section__list" data-faq-list>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">How do I remove the safe door? How much weight do I save?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Doors make up about 30% of the safe's total weight. Open the door 160–180 degrees, place a car jack on the bottom door plate or frame 0–8 inches from the hinge, and lift gently — the door rises about an inch before disengaging. This takes at least two people for smaller safes and four or more for larger ones. Do not attempt this on safes with three hinges.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">How do I move a safe up or down a large staircase?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">We recommend checking our forum thread on moving a safe down a full flight of stairs, where other owners share practical techniques and solutions.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">How do I load the safe on and off a pickup truck?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">We have a video demonstrating the proper loading technique — to unload, simply reverse the steps.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">How do I move a 400-700 pound safe?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Use two people and a hand truck rated for the weight. Moving Men Sliding Disks help a lot with pushing the safe across various surfaces.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">How do I move a 701-2000 pound safe?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Plan for three to five helpers. Moving Men Sliders, golf balls, pipes, pallet jacks, or specialized two-axle hand trucks can all help — evaluate which fits your specific situation best.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">How do I not crack the tile while moving the safe over it?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Improperly laid tile cracks easily. For properly laid tile, lay down plywood sheets to roll the safe over, using two large sheets and moving the front one ahead as you go to minimize material needed. Results aren't guaranteed, but this greatly improves your odds.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">How do I move a large or small safe off a pallet?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">We have a video demonstrating the proper technique for safely removing a safe from its pallet.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">Can you recommend any movers and installers?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Handymen often offer affordable hourly rates and creative solutions. Professional safe movers can be found through SAVTA (www.savta.org), and local safe distributors can also provide recommendations. We also keep a dedicated page listing highly-rated installers nationwide.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">How do I move a safe up or down a short staircase?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Build a sturdy ramp across the steps and use a heavy-duty Come-Along to pull the safe up. Tilting the safe back onto two corners lets you slide the ramp underneath.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-section__category">
      <h3 class="faq-section__category-title">Maintenance</h3>
      <div class="faq-section__list" data-faq-list>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">How do I maintenance the safe / vault? What oil do I use?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Use a Teflon-coated oil (we recommend a specific brand on our aftermarket accessories page). Never use WD-40 — it causes damage over time. Never oil the dial or locking mechanism itself. Oil the deadbolts when the handle bar fully exposes them, and oil the hinges through the top hole every four years. S&amp;G recommends annual locksmith maintenance, though most residential use needs it less often. Replace mechanical dials if problems arise, electronic S&amp;G D-Drive dials every 15 years, and other electronic locks every 10 years. To preserve the paint, touch up scratches and apply car wax periodically.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-section__category">
      <h3 class="faq-section__category-title">Bolting Down</h3>
      <div class="faq-section__list" data-faq-list>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">How should I bolt down a safe to a wood subfloor?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Bolt holes measure 11/16 inch in diameter; two bolts are needed. Use wood-anchoring bolts at least 3/8 inch thick, or 1/2-inch “All Thread” bolts through the floor. Pilot holes for lag screws shouldn't exceed 1/4 inch. Make the bolts long enough to go through the floor and secure underneath with cross members and large washers.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">How many anchor holes?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Two bolt-down locations are enough using 1/2"–5/8" diameter anchors, which provide superior grip. Newer safes have 3–4 holes (three for widths 36 inches or smaller, four for widths 42 inches or larger), though some 3/16-inch bodies still use two.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">How should I bolt down a safe to a concrete/cement floor?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Bolt holes measure 11/16 inch in diameter, with bolts approximately 1/2–5/8 inches thick. Fire-lined safes have 4-inch floors; non-insulated ones have 3/16-inch bodies. Every extra inch into concrete improves security — renting a roto hammer makes this easier. Two bolts are sufficient. Leave 1/4-inch of space on the front corners before drilling to ensure airflow. For outdoor safes, wax the exterior walls to prevent moisture. Several anchor bolt types work well — we have videos demonstrating installation, including forklift pull tests.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-section__category">
      <h3 class="faq-section__category-title">Shipping</h3>
      <div class="faq-section__list" data-faq-list>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">How long till I receive my safe or vault?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Manufacturing takes 1–9 weeks. Transit is estimated at seven business days for eastern states, 4–5 days for mid-states, and 1–3 days for western states — these are estimates, not guarantees, and the carrier ultimately schedules delivery. Storage beyond 3 days incurs daily fees.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">What happens if I change the delivery address after the safe is shipped?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Reconsignment fees and associated charges will apply, so please double-check your shipping address on your invoice before it ships.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">What am I to expect for the delivery?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">We have a video showing what to expect. Freight companies won't enter your home but may access your garage or exterior areas using a pallet jack — they don't move the safe off the pallet or unwrap it. A full-sized 48-foot truck is standard unless you request otherwise. If your location is hard to access (gravel drive, low trees, steep terrain), let us know in advance or plan for curbside delivery.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">What happens if there is freight damage?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">You'll receive shipping instructions and tracking by email. If there's damage, write “Freight Damaged. Refused Delivery” on the bill of lading and contact us before the driver leaves. We'll reship for free once it's resolved. Note that signing the shipping documents acknowledges the item arrived in good condition, so it's important to inspect before signing.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">How will the safe/vault be packaged in for shipping?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">The safe is wrapped, then double steel banded, and stands upright on a pallet. Vault doors ship the same way but laid down. Packaging is non-descriptive and marked “TOP HEAVY.”</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-section__item" data-faq-item>
          <div class="faq-section__header" data-faq-toggle>
            <p class="faq-section__question">Do you ship to Canada, Hawaii, or Alaska?</p>
            <span class="faq-section__toggle">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m19.5 8.25-7.5 7.5-7.5-7.5"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-section__body">
            <div class="faq-section__body-inner">
              <p class="faq-section__answer">Yes, but these require a phone quote since freight is specific to those regions. Canada also requires a broker to handle fees and duties separately — we can help assign one. Pricing may be higher than our standard online rates.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-section__category">
